.Dd October 7, 2026
.Dt AUTO-ROTATE-OSD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm auto-rotate-osd
.Nd show the autorotate glyph
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm on | off
.Op Ar hold_seconds
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
shows the autorotate glyph with
.Xr bosd 1 .
.Cm on
shows
.Cm auto-rotate-on .
.Cm off
shows
.Cm auto-rotate-off .
.Ar hold_seconds
is how many seconds the glyph stays up.
The default is 2.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "DISPLAY"
.It Ev DISPLAY
X server for
.Nm bosd .
The default is
.Pa :0 .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 1 when the mode is not
.Cm on
or
.Cm off .
When
.Nm bosd
is not installed,
the shell exits 127.
Otherwise it runs
.Nm bosd
and exits with that status.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr auto-rotate-disable 1 ,
.Xr auto-rotate-enable 1 ,
.Xr auto-rotate-toggle 1 ,
.Xr bhotkeys 1 ,
.Xr bosd 1 ,
.Xr framework_autorotate 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Devin Teske Aq Mt dteske@FreeBSD.org
